Void-specific instructions:
============================

greetd runs its greeter as the _greeter user on Void. Point it at the session
wrapper in /etc/greetd/config.toml:

  [default_session]
  command = "noctalia-greeter-session -- --session-wrapper dbus-run-session"
  user = "_greeter"

and restart greetd from a text console (this ends running sessions):

  sv restart greetd

Do not run /usr/share/noctalia-greeter/setup_greeter_system.sh or use the
output of noctalia-greeter-print-greetd-config: Void's /etc/pam.d/greetd
already gets pam_elogind from system-login, and Void's greetd uses vt = 7.

Options after "--" are passed to the greeter:

  --user NAME            open the password prompt for this user
  --session NAME         preselect a session (see: noctalia-greeter sessions)
  --session-wrapper CMD  start Wayland sessions through CMD (Void patch,
                         same as the tuigreet option)

Void's niri.desktop runs "/usr/bin/niri --session" without a D-Bus session bus,
so keep --session-wrapper dbus-run-session, as with tuigreet.

The greeter's compositor needs a seat: run elogind, or seatd with _greeter in
the _seatd group:

  usermod -aG _seatd _greeter

Settings and state live in /var/lib/noctalia-greeter, owned by _greeter.
Without /var/lib/noctalia-greeter/greeter.toml the defaults are used. Every key
is described in /usr/share/examples/noctalia-greeter/greeter.toml; its values
are only examples, so put just the keys you need into greeter.toml.
The keyboard layout is not read from /etc/rc.conf; set it in greeter.toml:

  [keyboard]
  layout = "us,ru"
  options = "grp:alt_shift_toggle"

Logs go to syslog (socklog-void). To log to a file instead:

  command = "env NOCTALIA_GREETER_LOG=/var/lib/noctalia-greeter/greeter.log noctalia-greeter-session -- --session-wrapper dbus-run-session"

Optional packages: accountsservice (user avatars), polkit (appearance sync
from Noctalia Shell), xinit (X11 sessions).
